  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let for any three distinct consecutive terms <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>c</mi></math> of an A.P, the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> be concurrent at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>)</mo></math> be a point such that the system of equations <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, has infinitely many solutions. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is equal to _______.</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "113",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></math> are in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now, on comparing above equation with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> we get,</p><p> The line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> passes through fixed point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Now, we know that for infinite solution,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>5</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>α</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p>And <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>6</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>β</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>5</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>α</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>So, the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>8</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>49</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>113</mn></math></p>"
  }
}